Usage: grid approve <task> [--plan-hash <hash>] [--gate plan|preview|ship] [--note <text>] [--json]
<task> is an id, exact folder name, or folder path inside a project tasks directory.
--plan-hash accepts the 6-hex plan_hash or 64-hex plan_digest from grid plan hash --json or grid task show --json.
workflow.md with plan_hash_token: digest requires the 64-hex digest.
--gate names the gate the person approved; a task now waiting at another gate is refused (exit 1) and nothing is written.
  -gate string
    	the gate the person approved: plan, preview or ship; refused when the task waits at another gate
  -json
    	print JSON
  -note string
    	approval note
  -plan-hash string
    	6-hex plan_hash or 64-hex plan_digest from grid plan hash --json or grid task show --json; workflow.md plan_hash_token: digest requires the digest
